                                               ADITYA BISHT
                      Agentic AI Engineer | Multi-Agent Systems | RAG & Tool Calling | LLM Evaluation
                 +91 7982759592 | New Delhi | aaditya85677@gmail.com | LinkedIn | GitHub | LeetCode | CodeChef

 SUMMARY
 Final-year B.Tech IT student (CGPA 8.60) who builds production-grade AI agents and the evals that prove they work. Shipped 4
 open-source frameworks (multi-agent orchestration, 8-strategy RAG, LoRA fine-tuning, LLM security), each live on HuggingFace
 with measured accuracy, latency and cost tradeoffs. At Synngular AI Labs, built multi-agent workflows with tool calling and
 human-in-the-loop gates, and deployed self-hosted LLMs behind a secured inference API. Treats LLM unreliability as a design
 constraint to evaluate and engineer around.
 EXPERIENCE
Prompt Engineering Intern â€” Synngular AI Labs                                                         Jun 2026 â€“ Sep 2026 | Remote
 â€¢ Built Project Atlas, a 4-agent workflow (inventory watch, PR approval, vendor scoring, RFQ generation) with per-plant scoping
   and external tool calls (MailGun), plus a 10-agent LangGraph planning system with human-in-the-loop approval gates.
 â€¢ Designed a Slack-integrated multi-agent system (Task Logger, Health Monitor, Meeting agents); benchmarked it against a
   single-agent design and shipped the architecture that held up on real workflows.
 â€¢ Benchmarked 3 agentic architectures (Single Agent, Planner+Implementor, Multi-Agent+Router) on a SQLite REST API spec
   using a 6-criterion weighted rubric (security, correctness, quality, spec compliance, robustness, efficiency). The Router passed
   16/16 surface tests yet scored lowest (~52%), exposing that platform-verifier scores were unreliable.
 â€¢ Deployed Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 and Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 on a DGX Spark (GB10) with vLLM: per-model tool-call parsers, FP8
   quantization and thinking mode off to speed up Cline, the team's coding agent. Secured the endpoint with a FastAPI gateway
   (API-key auth, Redis rate limiting), Caddy TLS and Cloudflare.
 â€¢ Built and tested CLI-based agent skills (SKILL.md, tool.json, strict skill-grounded execution) across docx, PDF and Next.js UI
   generation; documented gaps between platform docs and actual behavior.
 PROJECTS
AgentBench â€” Single vs Multi-Agent LLM Benchmarking Framework                                                    GitHub | Live Demo
 Python | LangGraph | Groq | FAISS | Tavily | SQLite | Streamlit | Plotly
 â€¢ Designed a 5-node pipeline (Planner, Researcher, Analyst, Writer, Memory) with Tavily tool calls, Pydantic structured outputs
   and SQLite agent memory; benchmarked 50 queries across 5 metrics and 2 agent configurations.
 â€¢ Built a resumable LLM-as-judge runner scoring 100 responses on accuracy, hallucination, relevance, latency and cost:
   multi-agent cut hallucination 6Ã— (24% â†’ 4%) at a 56Ã— latency cost (307s vs 5.5s).
 â€¢ Shipped a Streamlit dashboard with 7 live Plotly charts and 8 metric cards for real-time comparison.
RAG Systems Eval Suite â€” 8-Strategy RAG Benchmark Framework                                                      GitHub | Live Demo
 Python | FAISS | BM25 | LangChain | Groq | Cerebras | Streamlit | Pydantic
 â€¢ Benchmarked 8 strategies (Naive, Hybrid, Reranking, HyDE, Query Rewriting, Advanced, Adaptive, Base LLM) over 4,000
   answer-metric pairs (50 questions Ã— 8 systems Ã— 10 metrics).
 â€¢ FAISS + BM25/RRF hybrid search with cross-encoder reranking lifted faithfulness 16% (0.760 â†’ 0.881) and cut hallucination 4Ã—
   (0.816 â†’ 0.221).
 â€¢ Designed a dual-provider LLM-as-judge (Groq Llama-3.3-70B + Cerebras Llama-3.1-8B) with SQLite checkpoint/resume;
   published as an arXiv paper (cs.IR).
RAG Security Defense â€” Multi-Layer LLM Guardrails & Hybrid Retrieval                                             GitHub | Live Demo
 Python | Streamlit | Groq | ChromaDB | BM25 | Cross-Encoder Reranking | RBAC
 â€¢ Built a 5-layer defense pipeline that blocked 100% of 30 labeled attacks (15 regex injection + 15 jailbreak) at <1ms Layer-1
   latency, validated on a 100-query suite.
 â€¢ Implemented 4-stage hybrid retrieval (dense + BM25 + RRF k=60 + cross-encoder, 40 candidates to top-5) with 3-tier RBAC and
   0 cross-tier leaks.
CodeSage â€” LLM vs RAG vs Fine-Tuning Comparative AI Framework                                                    GitHub | Live Demo
 Python | LangChain | FAISS | HuggingFace PEFT | LoRA | Streamlit | Groq API
 â€¢ Fine-tuned Qwen2.5-1.5B with LoRA/PEFT: 85.3% accuracy at $0.0002/query with 0% hallucination, vs baseline LLM (43.2%
   hallucination) and RAG (0.768 answer relevance), quantifying the accuracy/cost/latency tradeoff.

 SKILLS
 Agentic AI: LangGraph, LangChain, CrewAI, MCP, Multi-Agent Systems, Tool/Function Calling, Planning & Reasoning, Agent
 Memory & State, Human-in-the-Loop, Agent Evaluation
 LLM / RAG: OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, Groq, Cerebras, vLLM, Prompt Engineering, Structured Outputs, Embeddings, Hybrid
 Search (BM25/RRF), Reranking, LoRA/PEFT, LLM-as-Judge, HuggingFace, PyTorch, TensorFlow
 Engineering: Python, FastAPI, REST APIs, Async, SQL, Redis, Docker, Git/GitHub, Linux, n8n
 Data & Cloud: ChromaDB, FAISS, Pinecone, SQLite; AWS (S3, EC2, Lambda), OCI, GitHub Actions (CI/CD), MLOps
 EDUCATION & CERTIFICATIONS
MAIT, GGSIPU â€” B.Tech Information Technology                                                              2023 â€“ 2027 | CGPA: 8.60
Kendriya Vidyalaya Janakpuri, CBSE                                                                Class 12: 88.2% | Class 10: 94.2%
 Oracle Cloud Infrastructure 2024: Generative AI Professional | AI Vector Search Professional

